WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:07.070
You asked — you got it.

2
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.710
The drop disappeared.

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.430
Recently I posted a TikTok in which I talk about an interesting drop

4
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.850
that is almost indestructible.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.490
And it did unexpectedly well.

6
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.790
What do you think, if I make a YouTube video about how I make and test it?

7
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.570
Yes, definitely make it. Yes, bro, make it. Come on.

8
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.730
Yes, bro, please. Come on, please.

9
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.610
Yes, makes sense. Do it. Yes, yes, yes.

10
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.650
This is Prince Rupert's drop.

11
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.790
It's made like this: molten glass is rapidly cooled in water.

12
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.490
When you work with glass, don't be stupid.

13
00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.330
Wear glasses. And gloves.

14
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.530
So, glass melts at a temperature of around 1400 degrees Celsius,

15
00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.570
and this torch can give a temperature above 1500 degrees Celsius,

16
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.590
so we're fine there.

17
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:59.020
Stop, I have everything, but I don't have glass.

18
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.960
This piece will be enough.

19
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.060
Let's try to make the first drop.

20
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.630
We melted one drop, let's see whether it worked.

21
00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.650
This is all that's left of the drop: unfortunately, it shattered.

22
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.670
Let's try again.

23
00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.650
I searched the internet and found out

24
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.570
that the glass I made this drop from is actually not suitable.

25
00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.610
You can't make this drop from such glass,

26
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.970
because it's not pure but has impurities to make it cheaper.

27
00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:36.010
So I ordered laboratory glass —

28
00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.030
those rods used for stirring in a chemistry lab.

29
00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.850
It turns out I broke that jar for nothing.

30
00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:42.850
Mom, sorry.

31
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.910
Now we just wait for these glass rods to arrive.

32
00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.010
Come on, subscribe quickly.

33
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.440
Besides the glass, I also bought this transparent water container,

34
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.500
so we can see the drop fall inside.

35
00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:07.820
Well, folks, looks like we have the first successful Prince Rupert's drop.

36
00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.200
No.

37
00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.260
On we go.

38
00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.980
And so I repeated and repeated the process and made drops

39
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.840
until I had six successful whole drops.

40
00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.160
Moving on to the first test.

41
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.560
Let's try to break it with pliers.

42
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.200
It's harder than I thought.

43
00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.220
The drop withstood the pliers.

44
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.820
Let's try something more powerful too.

45
00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.140
It shouldn't withstand this.

46
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.920
You know, I don't know how to hold it.

47
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.400
That is, it survived both the hammer blow and the fall from this vise.

48
00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.280
But the blow wasn't that strong.

49
00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.220
I want it like this, so that...

50
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:10.340
WTF?

51
00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.380
No way.

52
00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.600
The glass is even stronger than I thought.

53
00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.740
However, I ran into one problem.

54
00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.000
When you cut off this drop's tail, it should explode.

55
00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.620
But with my drop this didn't happen.

56
00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.900
Something even more interesting happened, but first let's move on to the next test.

57
00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.800
Since I don't have a hydraulic press,

58
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.340
I'll clamp this drop in a vise and squeeze with all my strength.

59
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.660
Let's see whether it holds.

60
00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.180
Needs to be even harder.

61
00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.530
No matter how hard I tried to squeeze it, the drop didn't even budge.

62
00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:47.170
But when I took the drop whose tail I'd cut off earlier,

63
00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.090
it burst.

64
00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.070
That means that, although it didn't explode by itself when I cut off the tail,

65
00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.210
it lost the property of indestructibility.

66
00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:58.270
That's why I said goggles are mandatory.

67
00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:01.090
But why is this drop indestructible at all?

68
00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.450
Let me explain a bit.

69
00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.130
To understand why the drop is strong at one end

70
00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.300
and fragile at the other, you need to look at how it forms.

71
00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.890
When molten glass falls into water,

72
00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.530
the outer layer of the drop cools sharply and contracts,

73
00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.110
while the inner part stays liquid for a longer time.

74
00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.270
And because of this, tension arises in the drop.

75
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.790
This energy is not released,

76
00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.770
and the drop is at every moment tensed like a spring.

77
00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.310
And only when the structure the drop has is disrupted,

78
00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.730
the energy is released, and the drop explodes.

79
00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.330
Which didn't happen with me.

80
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.630
And finally one more test that you'll definitely like.

81
00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:35.290
We will shoot at this drop with an air rifle.

82
00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.760
Don't try to repeat this at home,

83
00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.480
we're doing this under controlled conditions at my village estate.

84
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.760
In all other cases don't try it,

85
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.200
it's a really powerful air rifle.

86
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.200
You just saw the apple — there's your proof.

87
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.380
Now we'll try to blow the drop apart with this rifle,

88
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.260
let's see whether it's really indestructible.

89
00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.880
When I watched how foreign YouTubers filmed shooting at the drop,

90
00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.300
they hung the drop on fishing line.

91
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.380
Here's the drop that came out best of all,

92
00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.280
and now we'll tie it with fishing line and hang it here,

93
00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.880
let's see whether it can withstand a bullet from an air rifle.

94
00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.540
I think that hit the drop.

95
00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:24.060
Wow, dude, the drop disappeared.

96
00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.160
There's no drop.

97
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:30.360
Although it may seem that the drop was destroyed by the bullet, is that actually so?

98
00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:35.320
In this recording you see an ultra slow-motion shot of a real bullet hitting the drop.

99
00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:38.280
When the bullet hits the drop, nothing happens.

100
00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.340
However, the impact makes the tail start to vibrate.

101
00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.960
And only then do we notice the drop bursting.

102
00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.360
That means the head of the drop is strong enough to withstand a bullet's impact.

103
00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.880
So, I noticed that the drops I made

104
00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.200
differ quite a lot from the ones I'm comparing them with.

105
00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.000
So maybe I messed something up,

106
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.640
but judging by the tests, they were very strong.

107
00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.700
But in any case I'll definitely try to make them again someday

108
00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.380
and prepare even better tests.

109
00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.100
Thanks again for watching this video to the end.

110
00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.420
And I hope I lived up to your expectations.

111
00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:11.080
Don't forget to leave your support and subscribe for more videos like this.

112
00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:11.920
See you!